ARRAY SLICE - the manual's own example, on OPTION BASE 0
  a(2,*,3) = 203 213 223 233 243
  the blank index last
  a(1,2,*) = 120 121 122 123 124 125
  the blank index first
  a(*,4,5) = 45 145 245 345

MATH SLICE is the same command
  a(2,*,3) = 203 213 223 233 243

ARRAY INSERT puts one back
  a(2,0..4,3) = 900 901 902 903 904
  its neighbours are untouched: a(2,2,2)= 222 a(1,2,3)= 123
  a(1,2,0..5) = 700 701 702 703 704 705

float arrays
  f(1,*) = 1 1.1 1.2 1.3
  after insert f(1,2) = 99.5 f(0,2) = 0.2

string arrays
  s$(2,*) = C0 C1 C2 C3
  after insert s$(2,1) = zz  s$(1,1) = B1

a slice of a whole array through a SUB, where the rank is not
known until it is called
  x(3,3,*) = 330 331 332 333 334 335

COLOUR MAP - the array form of MAP()
  codes  = 0 3 6 9 12 15

